# Thothly — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` before running `docker-compose up`:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The MVP needs no API keys: YouTube uses native subtitles and blogs are
# read via RSS/scraping. Everything below has a sensible default.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Data directory (SQLite DB + generated EPUBs)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Inside Docker Compose the backend container mounts ./data at /data,
# so the default value below is correct and you do NOT need to set it.
# Override when running the backend directly on your host:
# DATA_DIR=./data
DATA_DIR=/data

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend URL (frontend → backend)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Override only if you run the frontend outside Docker Compose
# (e.g. `pnpm dev` on your host pointing at a remote backend).
# Inside docker-compose this is set to http://backend:8000 via the
# compose file and you do NOT need to set it here.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Web article search backend
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Which engine finds article URLs for a search query. Pluggable — pick one:
#
#   marginalia (DEFAULT, keyless) — indexes the independent "small web" (blogs,
#     docs, long-form), downranks SEO/commercial pages, and isn't rate-limited
#     to death like scraping DuckDuckGo. The "public" key needs no signup but
#     shares a tight rate limit; request a free personal key (email
#     contact@marginalia-search.com) for headroom. Free keys are CC-BY-NC-SA
#     (NON-commercial); a paid commercial key lifts that.
#   brave — broader general-web index, commercial-friendly, but needs an API key
#     (card on file) and is metered. Set WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND=brave + BRAVE_API_KEY.
#   ddg — legacy DuckDuckGo scrape; rate-limited hard, last-resort only.
#
# WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND=marginalia
# MARGINALIA_API_KEY=public
# BRAVE_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional LLM cleanup (transcript re-punctuation, copyedit, …)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave these EMPTY to keep Thothly fully zero-LLM (the default): punctuated
# captions are split into clean paragraphs for free, raw captions fall back to
# naive grouping. Set all three to enable the per-compilation "Nettoyage IA"
# roles in the review screen. One OpenAI-compatible endpoint covers every
# provider — just point base_url + model (+ key when the provider needs one).
#
# Local & free, with Ollama (`ollama pull llama3.1`):
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
# (no LLM_API_KEY needed)
#
# Mistral:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# OpenAI:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional speech-to-text (podcast episodes → transcript)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave these EMPTY to keep Thothly transcription-free: podcast episodes are
# then skipped (like a video with no subtitles), and many podcasts are anyway
# mirrored on YouTube, where native subtitles already cover them for free.
# Set all three to turn audio-only episodes into chapters. Same OpenAI-compatible
# shape as the LLM block — point base_url + model at any audio/transcriptions
# endpoint. Long episodes are split into <=25-min chunks, which needs `ffmpeg`
# installed (short episodes transcribe whole without it).
#
# Mistral Voxtral (recommended):
# STT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# STT_MODEL=voxtral-mini-latest
# STT_API_KEY=...
#
# Local & free (vLLM serving Voxtral-Mini-3B, or a whisper.cpp server):
# STT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# STT_MODEL=voxtral-mini
# (no STT_API_KEY needed)
